    "citation": "Wellman, C.H., Lopes, G., McKellar, Z. and Hartley, A. (2024). Age of the basal ‘Lower Old Red Sandstone’ Stonehaven Group of Scotland: the oldest reported air-breathing land animal is Silurian (late Wenlock) in age. Journal of the Geological Society, 181(1), jgs2023-138.",
    "language": "English",
    "reports_window_spores": true,
    "comment": "Table 1 compares an inland assemblage reused from Wellman (1993), A land plant microfossil assemblage of Mid Silurian age from the Stonehaven Group, Scotland, with a pooled assemblage from two new coastal samples. The authors support a late Wenlock (Homerian) age and dispute the Lochkovian interpretation of Suarez et al. (2017). Fig. 4f additionally illustrates an unidentified reticulate hilate cryptospore. The supplied DOI matches the article; live Crossref verification was unavailable."
